heir services, reach out to them immediately (within 24 hours if possible). \\n\\n2. **Set Up a Meeting**: Schedule a meeting/call with the client. The goal is to have a conversation about their reasons for cancellation. This should be a listening exercise, not a sales pitch to get them to stay.\\n\\n3. **Prepare for the Meeting**: Review the client&#x27;s file, understand their history with your company, and their reasons for signing up in the first place. \\n\\n4. **During the Meeting**: \\n    - Let them express their reasons for cancellation. \\n    - Ask open-ended questions to understand their concerns better.\\n    - Try to address any fixable issues or misunderstandings.\\n    - If there&#x27;s no chance of retention, proceed with the cancellation in a respectful and understanding manner.\\n\\n5. **Score Gathering**: \\n    - Ask the client to score their overall experience with your company.\\n    - Ask them to score their experience in the last 90 days.\\n    - Document these scores for future reference and to help identify potential areas for improvement.\\n\\n6. **Finalizing Cancellation**: \\n    - Have them sign the cancellation agreement. Make sure they understand the clauses that survive a cancellation.\\n    - Process their cancellation in your system.\\n    - Ensure all client data is handled as per your company&#x27;s data retention policy.\\n\\n7. **Post Cancellation**: Send them a farewell email thanking them for their business, expressing regret over their departure, and letting them know they&#x27;re welcome back anytime. \\n\\n### Questions to Ask:\\n- What prompted you to consider cancelling our services?\\n- Can you share any specific instances or experiences that led to this decision?\\n- Did our services meet your expectations?\\n- If you could change anything about our services, what would it be?\\n- Is there anything we could have done differently to prevent this cancellation?\\n- On a scale of 1-10, how would you rate your overall experience with us?\\n- On a scale of 1-10, how would you rate your experience with us in the last 90 days?\\n\\n## Cancellation Agreement \\n\\nThe cancellation agreement should be created by a legal professional as it has to meet certain legal standards and requirements, depending on the jurisdiction you operate in. However, a general template may look something like this:\\n\\n```Spanish\\nAcuerdo de Cancelaci\\u00f3n\\n\\nPor la presente confirmo que deseo cancelar los servicios de bookkeeping proporcionados por Servicios Rice-Velasquez.\\n\\nEntiendo y acepto que:\\n\\n1. Todas las obligaciones financieras pendientes hacia Servicios Rice-Velasquez deber\\u00e1n ser saldadas.\\n2. Cualquier cl\\u00e1usula en nuestro acuerdo inicial que se haya especificado para sobrevivir a una cancelaci\\u00f3n seguir\\u00e1 en efecto. Esto puede incluir, pero no est\\u00e1 limitado a, las obligaciones de confidencialidad y las restricciones de no competencia.\\n3. Servicios Rice-Velasquez retendr\\u00e1 mis datos de acuerdo con su pol\\u00edtica de retenci\\u00f3n de datos.\\n\\nNombre del Cliente: __________\\n\\nFirma del Cliente: __________\\n\\nFecha: __________\\n```\\n\\nThis should give you a starting point. Always make sure to consult with your legal counsel when creating or revising legal agreements. \\n\\n**My suggestion:** It could be beneficial to have a standardized internal form or software to document these conversations and scores. This data could be extremely helpful in identifying trends and areas for improvement.\\n\\nLet me know if you need more help with this."\highlight29\cf28\b ]\},\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "status"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "finished_successfully"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "end_turn"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight25\cf24\b\i0 true\highlight29\cf28\i0 ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "weight"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b