1098458.471429\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "update_time"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight25\cf24\b\i0 null\highlight29\cf28\i0 ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "content"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b \{\highlight27\cf26\b0 "content_type"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "text"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "parts"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b [\highlight27\cf26\b0 "**Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) for Client Cancellation**\\n\\nThis SOP provides detailed steps for handling client cancellation requests for the bookkeeping services offered by Servicios Rice-Velasquez. It aims to ensure that all cancellations are handled consistently, professionally, and in a manner that allows the company to understand the reasons behind the cancellations.\\n\\n**Purpose**\\n\\nThe purpose of this SOP is to outline the process for managing client cancellations effectively, ensuring that all necessary steps are taken and all information is adequately collected and documented.\\n\\n**Scope**\\n\\nThis SOP applies to all team members who deal with clients at any level, especially those in customer-facing roles such as customer service representatives, accountants, and client relationship managers.\\n\\n**Procedure**\\n\\n1. **Initial Contact**: Contact the client within 24 hours upon receiving a cancellation request. \\n\\n2. **Schedule a Meeting**: Arrange a conversation with the client to discuss their reasons for wanting to cancel.\\n\\n3. **Meeting Preparation**: Review the client&#x27;s history, previous issues, and service needs.\\n\\n4. **Conduct Meeting**: During the conversation, listen actively and ask open-ended questions. If issues can be addressed, attempt to resolve them. If not, proceed with the cancellation process.\\n\\n5. **Score Collection**: Ask the client to rate their overall experience and their experience in the last 90 days.\\n\\n6. **Finalize Cancellation**: Process the cancellation in your systems and have the client sign the cancellation agreement. \\n\\n7. **Post-Cancellation Follow-Up**: Send a follow-up email thanking the client for their business and leave the door open for future cooperation.\\n\\n**Questions to Ask During Cancellation Meeting**\\n\\nThese questions aim to provide insight into the client&#x27;s experience and reasons for cancellation:\\n\\n- What prompted your decision to cancel our services?\\n- Can you share specific experiences that led to this decision?\\n- Did our services meet your expectations?\\n- If you could change anything about our services, what would it be?\\n- Is there anything we could have done differently to prevent this cancellation?\\n- On a scale of 1-10, how would you rate your overall experience with us?\\n- On a scale of 1-10, how would you rate your experience with us in the last 90 days?\\n\\nThis SOP ensures that all client cancellations are handled in a respectful and informative way, allowing us to continuously improve our services based on client feedback.\\n\\n**My suggestion**: It might be beneficial to conduct periodic reviews of cancellation reasons and scores to identify recurring issues or trends and implement corrective measures."\highlight29\cf28\b ]\},\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "status"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "finished_successfully"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "end_turn"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight25\cf24\b\i0 true\highlight29\cf28\i0 ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "weight"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight21\cf20 1.0\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "metadata"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b \{\highlight27\cf26\b0 "finish_details"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf2