 documentation on behalf of La Fuente Cargo and is associated only with this point. All questions and concerns regarding the packages should be directed to La Fuente Cargo referencing their Guide Number on their form or receipt. The contact information for La Fuente Cargo can be found on their website: [www.lafuentecargo.com](www.lafuentecargo.com).\\n\\n**Definitions:**\\n- &quot;You,&quot; &quot;Your,&quot; and &quot;Client&quot; refer to the shipper and consignee.\\n- &quot;We,&quot; &quot;Our,&quot; and &quot;Us&quot; refer to La Fuente Cargo Corporation, its employees, and agents.\\n- &quot;Package,&quot; &quot;Shipment,&quot; and &quot;Freight&quot; refer to the cargo traveling under an invoice that can be transported by any means offered by La Fuente Cargo Corporation, including air, road, ship, or any other mode of transportation.\\n\\n**Agreement to Terms:**\\nBy entrusting us with your shipment, you accept, on behalf of yourself and any other person with an interest in this shipment, all the terms of this contract. Only authorized personnel of La Fuente Cargo Corporation can modify these Terms and Conditions.\\n\\n**Your Obligations:**\\nYou are responsible for properly packing your goods and accurately completing this contract, describing each item in the shipment, and providing correct contact information. Even if your shipment has already been paid for, you will also be responsible for any additional costs incurred by the company related to your shipment, such as fines, taxes, storage, and others.\\n\\n**Prohibited Items for Transportation:**\\nBy law, we are not allowed to transport any packages containing gold, diamonds, silver, money, personal checks, personal documents, liquor, explosives, weapons, drugs, and other restricted, hazardous, or prohibited items by United States customs or the countries we ship to.\\n\\n**Insurance:**\\nInsurance is optional and only applies to new items with a purchase invoice that justifies the declared value. If a client declines insurance, any claims will be handled at the company&#x27;s discretion with a maximum compensation value of $500.\\n\\n**Declared Value Limits:**\\nFor the contents of a shipment, regardless of the destination, the maximum declared value is US$1,000.\\n\\n**Delivery:**\\nDeliveries of the shipment will be made solely to the address indicated and to the specified recipient on your invoice. We will not deliver any package to third parties without the sender&#x27;s authorization. If your destination address is in a difficult or restricted access area, we will make the delivery to the nearest delivery point.\\n\\n**Claims:**\\nYou must submit all claims in writing within 7 days from the delivery of your package. If the recipient accepts your packages without indicating any anomalies on the delivery receipt, we determine that the package was delivered in good condition. We are not obligated to act on any claim until you have paid all transportation costs.\\n\\n**Our Rights:**\\nWe may, at our discretion and/or as requested by customs authorities, inspect your packages before or after they have been handed over to us for shipping. We reserve the right to take photographs of your shipment upon receipt and delivery for documentation, tracking, and promotional or educational purposes.\\n\\nPlease visit our website to view our **Full Terms and Conditions of Shipping**: [www.lafuentecargo.com/terminos-y-condiciones](www.lafuentecargo.com/terminos-y-condiciones)\\n\\nBy signing below, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to the terms outlined in this Drop Off Agreement Contract.\\n\\n---\\n\\nI hope this updated version meets your requirements. If you have any further requests or adjustments, please let me know, and I&#x27;ll be glad to assist you!"\highlight29\cf28\b ]\},\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "status"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "finished_successfully"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0 