lution, follow these steps:\\n\\n    - Navigate to https://make.powerapps.com and log in.\\n    - Select your environment at the top right.\\n    - Click on **Solutions** in the left sidebar.\\n    - Click **New Solution** at the top.\\n    - Fill out the necessary fields (display name, name, publisher, version) and click **Create**.\\n\\n2. **Create a new custom entity:**\\n\\n    Entities in Dynamics 365 are like database tables that store records. You&#x27;ll create a new entity to store each asylum application.\\n\\n    - Inside your solution, click on **New** and select **Entity**.\\n    - Fill out the necessary fields (display name, plural name, name, primary field). \\n    - The primary field could be something like &quot;Application ID&quot; and will be automatically created by Dynamics.\\n    - Click **Next** and then **Create**.\\n\\n3. **Create custom fields:**\\n\\n    Fields in Dynamics 365 are like columns in a database table. You&#x27;ll create fields for each question in the asylum form.\\n\\n    - Inside your custom entity, click on **Fields** in the left sidebar.\\n    - Click **Add Field** at the top.\\n    - Fill out the necessary fields (display name, name, data type).\\n    - Repeat this process for each question in the asylum form.\\n    - Click **Save Entity** in the bottom right.\\n\\n4. **Create a new form:**\\n\\n    Forms in Dynamics 365 are what users interact with to enter and view data. You&#x27;ll create a form to input and view each asylum application.\\n\\n    - Inside your custom entity, click on **Forms** in the left sidebar.\\n    - Click **New Form** at the top.\\n    - Drag and drop the fields you created earlier from the field explorer (right sidebar) onto the form.\\n    - Click **Save** and then **Publish** at the top.\\n\\nWith these steps, you should have a custom solution with an entity that corresponds to the asylum application form. You can then enter data into this entity manually through the Dynamics 365 interface, or