 &quot;If&quot;.\\n11. In the condition, tap &quot;Choose&quot; and select &quot;Text&quot;. Then tap the second &quot;Choose&quot; and select &quot;Input&quot;. Now you should see &quot;If Text Input&quot;. Tap on &quot;Input&quot; and type the specific message you&#x27;re expecting, e.g., &quot;Ding Dong&quot;.\\n12. After setting up the condition, tap &quot;Add Action&quot; below the &quot;Then&quot; statement.\\n13. You can now select what you want to happen if the condition is met. For example, if you want to play a sound, you could select &quot;Play Sound&quot;. If you want to send a reply, you could select &quot;Send Message&quot;, etc.\\n14. Once you&#x27;ve set up your action, tap &quot;Next&quot;.\\n15. Review the automation. Make sure &quot;Ask Before Running&quot; is turned off to ensure the automation runs automatically. Then tap &quot;Done&quot;.\\n\\nThis automation should now run whenever you receive a message from the selected contact. If the message matches the specific text you set, it will perform the action(s) you specified.\\n\\nPlease note that due to privacy and security reasons, Apple might not allow direct triggering of automations based on message content. The options available to you might also depend on the updates and changes Apple has made to the Shortcuts app and iOS since my knowledge cutoff in September 2021. Please refer to the most recent user manuals or help resources for the best results."\highlight29\cf28\b ]\},\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "status"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "finished_successfully"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "end_turn"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight25\cf24\b\i0 true\highlight29\cf28\i0 ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "weight"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight21\cf20 1.0\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "metadata"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \high