4252\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "update_time"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight25\cf24\b\i0 null\highlight29\cf28\i0 ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "content"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b \{\highlight27\cf26\b0 "content_type"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "text"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "parts"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b [\highlight27\cf26\b0 "Summary Recommendation:\\n\\nBased on the information gathered, it is crucial to proceed with caution when considering establishing residency in Florida while keeping your business in Indiana. While Florida offers the advantage of no state income taxes, attempting to claim residency in Florida solely for tax purposes can lead to complications and potential legal consequences.\\n\\nDual State Residency: It is important to be aware that claiming residency in another state to avoid tax penalties can result in dual taxation, where you may be taxed by both states. This can create complexities and increase the likelihood of audits or inquiries from tax authorities.\\n\\nResidency Requirements: To establish residency in Florida, you must be physically present in the state for at least 183 days of the tax year. It is also beneficial to establish a domicile in Florida, including obtaining a driver&#x27;s license, registering your vehicle, and owning a home in the state.\\n\\nTax Fraud and Penalties: It is crucial to emphasize that intentionally misrepresenting your residency for tax purposes can be considered tax fraud, which is illegal. Both criminal and administrative penalties can be imposed, including fines and potential jail time.\\n\\nConsult with a Tax Professional: Given the complexity and potential risks involved, I strongly recommend consulting with a qualified tax professional or accountant who specializes in multi-state taxation. They will be able to provide personalized guidance based on your specific circumstances and help you navigate the tax implications of your residency and business location.\\n\\nMaintaining Accurate Records: It is important to keep meticulous records of your time spent in each state, including travel and accommodation documents, to support your residency claims and ensure compliance with tax laws.\\n\\nIn conclusion, while the idea of using your Florida residence as the primary legal address for tax purposes may seem appealing due to the absence of state income taxes, it is essential to thoroughly evaluate the potential risks and consult with a tax professional. Compliance with tax laws and avoiding fraudulent activities should always be a priority to prevent serious legal and financial consequences."\highlight29\cf28\b ]\},\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "status"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "finished_successfully"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "end_turn"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight25\cf24\b\i0 true\highlight29\cf28\i0 ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "weight"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight21\cf20 1.0\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "metadata"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b \{\highlight27\cf26\b0 "finish_details"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b \{\highlight27\cf26\b0 "type"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "stop"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "stop"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "&lt;|diff_marker|&gt;"\highlight29\cf28\b \},\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "is_complete"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight25\cf24\b\i0 true\highlight29\cf28\i0 ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "message_type"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight25\