ighlight27\cf26 "create_time"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight21\cf20 1688312120.359525\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "update_time"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight25\cf24\b\i0 null\highlight29\cf28\i0 ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "content"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b \{\highlight27\cf26\b0 "content_type"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "text"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "parts"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b [\highlight27\cf26\b0 "Absolutely! It sounds like a very sensible move to centralize all your company&#x27;s knowledge into one platform. Here&#x27;s a basic roadmap that can guide you through the process of creating SOPs (Standard Operating Procedures) and updating your knowledge base within Microsoft Dynamics 365:\\n\\n1. **Audit Current Materials:** Identify the location of all your current documents, drafts, SharePoint Learning Center materials, HTML links, etc. Create a master list of these resources, including details such as their subject matter, last updated date, and any gaps or redundancies.\\n\\n2. **Categorize your Knowledge Base:** Determine the different categories of knowledge that your company needs. This could be things like product information, customer service protocols, technical support guides, etc. This step will make it easier for your team to find information later.\\n\\n3. **Set up Knowledge Articles in Dynamics 365:** Dynamics 365 allows you to create knowledge articles which can be used to share information with your team. You can categorize these articles according to the categories you determined earlier.\\n\\n4. **Create a Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) Template:** A SOP is a detailed, step-by-step instruction guide designed to help your team carry out complex tasks accurately and consistently. Create a template for your SOP