ot;Insert&quot; &gt; &quot;Icons&quot; &gt; &quot;Loading Spinner&quot;. Position this spinner on your screen where you want it to appear. Set its &quot;Visible&quot; property to a variable (e.g., `varLoading`) that will control when it&#x27;s visible.\\n\\n2. **Show Spinner When Submitting**: On your &quot;Submit&quot; button, you will need to modify the &quot;OnSelect&quot; action to first set `varLoading` to `true` before the form submission begins:\\n\\n```PowerApps\\nSet(varLoading, true);\\nSubmitForm(yourForm);\\n```\\n\\n3. **Hide Spinner After Submitting**: After the form has been submitted, you can use the &quot;OnSuccess&quot; action of your form to hide the spinner and show the notification:\\n\\n```PowerApps\\nSet(varLoading, false);\\nNotify(&quot;Your form has been submitted. You may now close the app.&quot;, NotificationType.Success);\\n```\\n\\nThis will ensure that the spinner is visible while the form is submitting and becomes hidden after the submission is complete. Additionally, the user is notified that they can now close the app.\\n\\nNote: Replace &quot;yourForm&quot; with the name of your form control. Also, the spinner and the &quot;Notify&quot; function rely on the form submission to be somewhat instantaneous. If you have a significant delay or need to handle possible errors in the form submission, you may need a more complex setup."\highlight29\cf28\b ]\},\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "status"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "finished_successfully"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "end_turn"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight25\cf24\b\i0 true\highlight29\cf28\i0 ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "weight"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight21\cf20 1.0\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "metadata"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b \{\highlight27\cf26\b0 "message_type"\highlight29\cf2