ght29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "text"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "parts"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b [\highlight27\cf26\b0 "In Power Automate, you can use the following expression to get the previous month&#x27;s name as text:\\n\\n```plaintext\\nformatDateTime(addMonths(utcNow(), -1), &#x27;MMMM&#x27;)\\n```\\n\\nHere&#x27;s what it does:\\n\\n- `utcNow()` gets the current date and time in UTC format.\\n- `addMonths(utcNow(), -1)` subtracts one month from the current date and time.\\n- `formatDateTime()` formats the resulting date to a specific format. In this case, &#x27;MMMM&#x27; will return the full name of the month.\\n\\nThis will return the full name of the previous month. For example, if the current month is July, the expression would return &quot;June&quot;."\highlight29\cf28\b ]\},\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "status"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "finished_successfully"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "end_turn"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight25\cf24\b\i0 true\highlight29\cf28\i0 ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "weight"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight21\cf20 1.0\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "metadata"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b \{\highlight27\cf26\b0 "message_type"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight25\cf24\b\i0 null\highlight29\cf28\i0 ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "model_slug"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "gpt-4"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "finish_details"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight29\cf28\b \{\highlight27\cf26\b0 "type"\highlight29\cf28\b :\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "stop"\highlight29\cf28\b ,\highlight17\cf16\b0  \highlight27\cf26 "stop"\highlight29\c